{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the sense of 'with evil he brought them out'.</b> As our earlier Sages of blessed memory hinted, that they came out of Egypt under an evil constellation, and [the nations] will say there is no power in HaShem to overcome the force of the constellation to save those who cleave to Him, and when He saw that He had no power, He killed them — and this would be a profanation of the Name. Now he fell [in prayer] forty days, and HaShem said to him, 'I will not go up in your midst' (below, 33:3), and [that] they would not inherit the land. Then Moses said the entire passage of 'See, you say to me' (ibid. v. 12), and afterward HaShem commanded him to go down and hew tablets and bring them up in his hand to the mountain. Then HaShem descended in a cloud and the skin of his face radiated, and HaShem wrote the second tablets. Therefore it is written: 'At that time HaShem said to me: Hew for yourself two tablets of stone like the first' etc., 'and make for yourself an ark of wood' (Deuteronomy 10:1). And Israel would make the ark — and it is [the one] that Bezalel made."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:45.196425334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}